        {
            ["updateLogId"] = 250,
            ["visible"] = true,
            ["title"] = "BedWars\' Anniversary + Warrior Kit Returns",
            ["date"] = "05/22/2026",
            ["body"] = "\226\154\148\239\184\143 <b>Warrior Kit Returns</b>\nWarrior is making its return as part of our efforts to let players experience some of BedWars\226\128\153 older legacy kits. We know Warrior originally came from a Battle Pass and we understand that some players value owning it from its original release. To respect that, players who unlocked Warrior during its original Battle Pass will receive a Limited \226\128\156OG Warrior Chroma\226\128\157.\nOur goal is to bring back older gameplay content in a way that lets newer players enjoy these kits while still respecting the players who have earned them from when they first released.\n\n\240\159\141\176 <b>BedWars\226\128\153 Anniversary Event</b>\nFor a limited time, there will be a cake that players can eat in the base. When player eats cake they get a random buff!\n- Balloons and snowballs replace the rotating limited time items for classic queues\n- Party Hats on players and in-game entities!\n\n\240\159\140\136 <b>Anniversary (Armor Trim Effect)</b> \nObtain the new flashy Anniversary Armor Trim Effect through the Lucky Crates!\n\n<b>\240\159\146\170 Warrior Rework</b>\n- Removed shop discount and damage reduction\n<b>New Mechanic: Grit & Final Stand</b>\n- <b>Grit Generation:</b> Warrior gains <b>Grit</b> by dealing or taking damage from sword and arrow.\n- <b>Final Stand:</b> Upon taking fatal damage, Warrior defies death and enters a <b>Final Stand</b>. While in this state, Grit continuously decays and absorbs all incoming damage. Warrior remains active until their Grit is completely depleted.\n- On Warrior armor and Emerald Armor, If Warrior gets a kill during <b>Final Stand</b>, they immediately exit the state and convert all remaining Grit into Health, escaping death.\n<b>Active Ability: Warrior\226\128\153s Strike</b>\nThe effects of this ability scale based on Warrior\'s current <b>Grit</b>:\n- <b>Low Grit (less than than 50):</b> Deals damage to nearby enemies and gain Grit for each enemy hit.\n- <b>High Grit (50\226\128\14799):</b> Consumes 50 Grit to deal damage to nearby enemies and grants a shield for each enemy hit.\n- <b>Max Grit (100):</b> Consumes all Grit to deal massive damage in a larger radius and heals Warrior for each enemy hit.\n- <b>During Final Stand:</b> Automatically triggers the <b>Max Grit</b> version with increased damage, but no longer heals.\nWarrior ignores knockback and gain 30% damage reduction while using the ability.\n<b>Warrior Armor:</b>\n- Warrior\226\128\153s diamond armor is replaced with Warrior armor.\n- Warrior armor has increased defense and gain 3 extra grit when taking damage.\n\n<b>\240\159\145\145 Warrior Kit and Skin Bundle</b>\nAvailable in the store for 999 robux (1398 robux value)!\nThe bundle includes:\n\n\240\159\148\147 <b>Ice Viking Warrior (Kit Skin)</b> - (799 robux value)\nThe Warrior kit and future Battle Pass kit releases will be sold individually for 599 robux or 25,000 BedCoins after 2 weeks.\n\n\240\159\140\140 <b>Celestial Zephyr Kit Skin</b>\nAvailable in the store for 799 robux!\n\n\226\154\150\239\184\143 <b>Ranked Changes</b>\nAfter feedback on Season 16 RP, we made some changes so that RP more drastically changes by who you\226\128\153re playing against (for example, winning against someone much <b>higher</b> rated gives you more RP, and losing to someone much <b>lower</b> rated takes away more RP). Additionally, we\226\128\153ve committed to making higher ranks (especially Emerald 1 and up) more difficult to climb.\nBecause it\226\128\153s now more difficult to climb in higher ranks, this update re-scales all players who are currently <b>Emerald 1 and up</b> so there\226\128\153s less of a gap between top players. This makes it more fair for anyone who wasn\226\128\153t able to climb Emerald and Nightmare ranks under the easier RP system. Re-scaling drops RP proportionally, so the current number 1 player on the leaderboard will still be number 1 after re-scaling. If you\226\128\153re not currently Emerald 1 or higher, you are not affected by the re-scaling.\nPlayers will now receive ranked rewards for the <b>highest rank</b> they earn during ranked season 16, instead of the rank they end with. This means that if you reach Gold 1, but continue to play and end the season at Silver 2, you will receive Gold rewards. This excludes Nightmare, which represents the current top 200 players over 2400 RP.\n\n<b>\240\159\134\147 Free Kits</b>\n\240\159\146\142Drill\n\240\159\144\136Yamini\n\226\173\144Star Collector Stella\n\240\159\151\161\239\184\143Caitlyn (Player level 20 unlock)\n\n\240\159\148\167 <b>Other Changes</b>\n- Easter Event has been disabled.\n\240\159\166\180 Marrow Kit Price Reduced: 479 Robux \226\134\146 399 Robux or 12,000 BedCoins \226\134\146 10,000 BedCoins\n\240\159\148\171 Zarrah Kit Price Reduced: 479 Robux \226\134\146 399 Robux or 12,000 BedCoins \226\134\146 10,000 BedCoins\n\240\159\145\187 Zola Kit Purchasable in store: 479 Robux or 12,000 BedCoins\n\n\240\159\144\155 <b>Bug Fixes</b>\n- Fixed inconsistent ranked RP gains and losses\n",
